  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    Substance use patterns among men 35–60 are frequently invisible in plain sight —
    two to four drinks nightly, habitual caffeine overdependence, nicotine, or recreational
    substances used to manage the stress and sleep deficits that accumulate in this life stage.
    These patterns erode metabolic health, hormones, sleep architecture, and cognitive function
    while being socially normalized.
  </p>
  <p>
    My4MLife does not offer addiction treatment. What we offer is an honest, non-shaming
    framework for assessing how substance use is interacting with your health goals and
    a structured behavioral pathway to reduce habitual dependence patterns.
  </p>

  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Honest Inventory</h3>
      <p>Structured self-assessment covering frequency, quantity, context, and function — no judgment, just data.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Upstream Root Causes</h3>
      <p>Most habitual use is a coping mechanism for stress, poor sleep, or social isolation. Address those first.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Replacement Protocol</h3>
      <p>Behavioral substitutions that meet the same need — relaxation, social bonding, stimulation — without the metabolic cost.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Referral Pathway</h3>
      <p>We maintain relationships with evidence-based addiction specialists and telehealth MAT providers for individuals who need more support.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</SolutionPage>
